@overheard commons
// Writer-commons, overheard batch 1. The garden, the store, the infirmary and the galley, by the people who work there.

== overheard
? pair:garden+any place:hydroponics_garden
A: Who's been picking the flowers?
B: Couldn't say.
A: There's a gap in the row.
B: Must have been the misters.   #funny

? pair:any+garden
A: When are the tomatoes ready?
B: Week twelve. Not a day sooner.

? pair:store+any place:crew_store
A: You've run out of soap.
B: How do you know that?
A: I know everything.   #funny

? pair:any+store place:crew_store
A: Do you have any of the good biscuits?
B: Gone by nine. Every day.
A: Who buys them all?
B: I never say.

? pair:infirmary+any
A: Have you had water today?
B: I had tea.
A: Tea isn't water.
B: It's mostly water.   #funny

? pair:galley+galley act:work
A: Six trays.
B: Show off.
A: Seven tomorrow.   #funny

? pair:galley+galley act:work
A: Cold store's up two degrees.
B: Don't tell Brennan.
A: Too late. She heard.
B: Run.   #funny

? pair:galley+any time:evening
A: There's a plate on the grab shelf.
B: Whose?
A: Whoever needs it most.   #warm
